# Cluster and positioning admission audit

Reviewer: fresh native gpt-6-sol High, `/root/cluster_position_admission_audit`. Read-only source and existing evidence review; no tests, builds, benchmarks or product edits.

At frozen product `dec7509b3a18b2d71e27de023419f45c32fb10e7`, the dense text edit does not show more avoidable semantic work than main `4e25a96a57462fef5ad0d19065a822695b480f60`. Current `packages/glyph/rust/shaper/src/engine/state.rs:5290` detects a single full source run with one grapheme per UTF-16 unit and builds clusters directly. Main instead attempts `rebuild_source_run_if_topology_is_stable`. If admitted, that path copies the old cluster arena and visits every glyph twice because the source run owns the entire paragraph. Main's admission on this exact replay remains unmeasured; if it rejects, main falls back to a full build. There is no source-backed reason to replace the current full builder.

The authenticated ledger `benches/reports/held-row-view-local-2026-10-21/native/bitmap-native-work-ledger.json.raw` records, for each forward and reverse phase across 1,024 paragraphs: 1,024 HarfRust calls, 1,024 full cluster builds, 10,240 full cluster glyph visits, zero retained cluster glyph visits and old cluster rows copied, 1,024 recomposed flow lines, 10,240 newly positioned semantic glyphs, and zero copied positioned records. These are native preparation work counts, not timings or the 9,216 rendered glyphs. The ledger authenticates its historical source, not a new timing of dec7509b3.

Text edits exclude the geometry-only retained-flow gate in current state.rs:5961 and main state.rs:4790. Each paragraph has one recomposed line, leaving no clean line for either positioning builder to copy. The replay `benches/labs/package/bitmap-native-replay.capture.mts:205`, stress benchmark `stress.bench.ts:124`, and profile `edit-sized-publication.profile.mts:223` use the same createTextBatch text pattern and alternate alpha/bravo with a four-digit suffix. Each string is ten UTF-16 units, including the space. The earlier nine-unit description was incorrect; this does not equate native source rows and rendered instances or establish complete fixture/artifact equivalence by itself.

If main branch admission becomes consequential, the smallest additional observation is a test-only success count for main's retained source-run rebuild on the exact replay. Main lacks the newer work_attribution counters. Existing current counters already settle the current branch. No runtime optimization or latency benefit follows from this source audit.
